(Q49) A travel company recommends holiday packages based on budget, number of travellers, and travel preference.
•	Budget below ₹15,000: Local package.
•	Budget ₹15,000–₹40,000: Domestic package.
•	Budget ₹40,001–₹1,00,000: International budget package.
•	Budget above ₹1,00,000: Luxury international package.
•	Families travelling with more than four members receive a 10% group discount.
•	Solo travellers receive a 5% discount.
•	If the selected package exceeds the customer's budget after calculating the discount, display an alternative package recommendation.
Write a Python program to recommend a travel package and calculate the discounted package price.

budget = float(input("Enter total budget: "))
travellers = int(input("Enter number of travellers: "))
preference = input("Travel preference (adventure/relaxation): ").lower()
if budget < 15000:
    package = "Local"
    cost = 12000
elif budget <= 40000:
    package = "Domestic"
    cost = 35000
elif budget <= 100000:
    package = "International Budget"
    cost = 85000
else:
    package = "Luxury International"
    cost = 150000
if travellers > 4:
    discount = 10
elif travellers == 1:
    discount = 5
else:
    discount = 0
final_cost = cost - (cost * discount / 100)
if final_cost <= budget:
    print("Recommended Package:", package)
    print("Travel Preference:", preference)
    print("Discount:", discount, "%")
    print("Package Cost: ₹", final_cost)
